From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kirill <sleeply4cat@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:59:27 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 13/26] ASoC: codecs: lpass-va-macro: accept LPASS codec v2.1
 and v2.2

SM6225 uses the sm6115 compatible, and its VA macro reports v2.2.0, so
probe fails with -EOPNOTSUPP. The stock DT calls this Bolero 2.1, and
the macros already handle that version together with 2.0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015ya7egg5XM6dMvKwj1kAyq
---
 sound/soc/codecs/lpass-va-macro.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-va-macro.c b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-va-macro.c
index dbc5795b9..d67b10514 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-va-macro.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-va-macro.c
@@ -1508,6 +1508,10 @@ static int va_macro_set_lpass_codec_version(struct va_macro *va)
 		case 0:
 			version = LPASS_CODEC_VERSION_2_0;
 			break;
+		case 1:
+		case 2:
+			version = LPASS_CODEC_VERSION_2_1;
+			break;
 		case 5:
 			version = LPASS_CODEC_VERSION_2_5;
 			break;
-- 
2.43.0

